The wrapper creates fresh digit domains, runs propagation, and returns either the reduced domains or None. This implementation initializes variables from the first position of each constraint tuple; the example includes every variable there.

def solve(constraints: List[Tuple[str, str, int]]):
    domains = {x: list(range(10)) for x in set(x for x, _, _ in constraints)}
    if ac3(constraints, domains):
        return domains
    return None

